{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"The derivative $f'(x)$ of a function $(f)$ at a point $(x)$ can be viewed as the steepness and direction, or slope, of the function's graph at that point.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"Here we see the steepness and direction of the graph of $f$ at the point where $x=0$:\n\n![graph](web+graphie:${☣ LOCALPATH}/images/377e5a7e11ee1201478a6a41b03d69427f78f085)","images":{"web+graphie:${☣ LOCALPATH}/images/377e5a7e11ee1201478a6a41b03d69427f78f085":{"height":425,"width":425}},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"We can see that the graph is constant at $x=0$, which means the slope must be equal to $0$.\n","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"In conclusion, $f'(0)=0$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"**Estimate $f'(0)$.**\n\n[[☃ radio 1]]\n\n![graph](web+graphie:${☣ LOCALPATH}/images/ab140adb7b6af72100bf828826e42183d088fba6)","images":{"web+graphie:${☣ LOCALPATH}/images/ab140adb7b6af72100bf828826e42183d088fba6":{"height":425,"width":425}},"widgets":{"radio 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"choices":[{"content":"$0.5$","correct":false},{"content":"$0$","correct":true},{"content":"$-0.5$","correct":false,"isNoneOfTheAbove":false},{"content":"$2$","correct":false,"isNoneOfTheAbove":false},{"content":"$-2$","correct":false,"isNoneOfTheAbove":false}],"deselectEnabled":false,"displayCount":null,"hasNoneOfTheAbove":false,"multipleSelect":false,"onePerLine":false,"randomize":true},"static":false,"type":"radio","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
